---
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_GITHUB_URL, SITE_INSTAGRAM_URL, SITE_LINKEDIN_URL, SITE_ROLE, SITE_TITLE, SITE_X_URL } from "../consts";
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";

const personJsonLd = JSON.stringify({
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "Person",
	name: SITE_TITLE,
	url: Astro.site?.toString(),
	description: SITE_DESCRIPTION,
	jobTitle: SITE_ROLE,
	address: { "@type": "PostalAddress", addressLocality: "Madrid", addressCountry: "ES" },
	sameAs: [SITE_LINKEDIN_URL, SITE_GITHUB_URL, SITE_X_URL, SITE_INSTAGRAM_URL],
	knowsAbout: ["Infrastructure", "Virtualization", "Proxmox", "Linux", "Windows Server", "Networking", "Self-hosting", "Local LLM inference"],
});

const chapters = [
	{
		age: "6",
		title: "The first website.",
		text: "Before I could explain what a server was, I wanted one. The website came first, and with it the habit of taking things apart to see how they run.",
	},
	{
		age: "8",
		title: "Minecraft servers.",
		text: "Plugins in Java, which I hated. But it was the first time I cared more about how the server worked than what I was building on top of it. The systems instinct was there before I had a name for it.",
	},
	{
		age: "13",
		title: "TypeScript and Discord bots.",
		text: "By thirteen I had most of the technical foundations I still carry. Code that other people actually used, and broke, and needed fixed.",
	},
	{
		age: "15",
		title: "Turing AI.",
		text: "Product and community manager for an AI product with <b>767,000+ users</b>, later acquired by shapes.inc. I turned what people told us into fixes, and helped put the AI APIs behind RabbitMQ load balancing so the service held up while it grew.",
	},
	{
		age: "17",
		title: "Burnout, then the homelab.",
		text: "Then burnout hit. A hard stop. The homelab brought me back: a Proxmox cluster built from hardware other people retired, running my own Matrix and Nextcloud and local AI. Fixing real errors on real machines, with real consequences, fixed something in me too. Around the same time I built servers at Ibertronica, testing every one before it shipped.",
	},
	{
		age: "18",
		title: "Abalun, and the paper trail.",
		text: "Practice hours at Abalun pulled me into real work fast enough that the line blurred: sites in Webflow and Elementor, schemas and migrations in MySQL and PostgreSQL. What it mostly did was kill the impostor syndrome. Turns out the impostor was the lie, not me. The CFGM in Microcomputer Systems and Networks made it official in June 2026.",
	},
];
---

<Site title="About" description={`Madrid born and raised. ${SITE_ROLE}. The full story, from a first website at six to a homelab that never sleeps.`}>
	<script is:inline slot="head" type="application/ld+json" set:html={personJsonLd} />

	<section class="story-hero">
		<a class="back" href="/">← Back home</a>
		<span class="lbl">About · the full story</span>
		<h1 class="cond story-title">The full<br />story.</h1>
		<p class="story-lead">Madrid born and raised. {SITE_ROLE}. ADHD, Asperger's, gifted. Building things that close the gap between people and what they need.</p>
	</section>

	<section class="sec chapters" aria-label="Chapters">
		{
			chapters.map((c) => (
				<article class="chapter">
					<div class="age"><span class="cond">{c.age}</span><span class="lbl">years old</span></div>
					<div class="ch-body"><h2>{c.title}</h2><p set:html={c.text} /></div>
				</article>
			))
		}
		<article class="chapter now">
			<div class="age"><span class="cond">Now</span><span class="lbl">2026</span></div>
			<div class="ch-body">
				<h2>Choosing the next room.</h2>
				<p>I'm looking for infrastructure work with people who care how things run, in Madrid or remote. Moxen, my control plane for AI coding agents, is taking shape on the side.</p>
				<a class="btn btn-blue" href="#contact">Hire me ↗</a>
			</div>
		</article>
	</section>

	<section class="sec thread">
		<span class="lbl">The thread</span>
		<blockquote class="cond">The distance between people and what they need is always smaller than it looks.</blockquote>
		<p>Every project I build closes that gap a little. A scheduler that stops a manager carrying the week in their head. An AI that shows up where your people already are. A phone that stops gatekeeping your own life. Music pulls at me for the same reason: a good song doesn't create emotion, it removes what's in the way of it.</p>
	</section>

	<section class="sec trio">
		<article>
			<span class="lbl">Writing</span>
			<h3>How I think.</h3>
			<p>I'll type three paragraphs to understand one sentence. I want to write about whatever I'm trying to understand: systems, neurodivergence as it's lived, the parts of a person that don't fit on a CV. First essay: being present, and nostalgia.</p>
		</article>
		<article>
			<span class="lbl">Music</span>
			<h3>Side B.</h3>
			<p>Learning to produce and to sing. Early days, solid foundations, and a first instrumental you can already play on the home page.</p>
			<a class="more" href="/#sides">Play “it's complicated” ↗</a>
		</article>
		<article>
			<span class="lbl">Madrid</span>
			<h3>Home, for now.</h3>
			<p>The place that made me, and the people I love most are here. But I've started to feel the edges. One day I'll find out what happens when I leave. Until then: Madrid, and open to remote.</p>
		</article>
	</section>
</Site>
